Arthur J. O'Dwyer wrote:
> 
> On Mon, 11 Dec 2006, Simon Richard Clarkstone wrote:
>> Arthur J. O'Dwyer wrote:
> 
>> You know, this would work far better if there was a proper "ownership" 
>> system.
> 
>   Yes. Then when a nymph steals your sword, you can wish for "my sword"
> and get it back. (Actually, another improvement for my current patch is
> to let "sword" match "long sword", and so on.)
> 
> -Arthur

An ownership system already exists -- its called Naming. I always name 
certain items in my inventory; for example my pickaxe is always named 
Digger. (Then if stolen by foo monster, when I kill the little cretin I 
know the items' b/u/c status.)

I think this would cause more players to name their items. And, as is 
the RNGs tendency, the foo monster would probably steal the non-named 
item first. Don't name your items, you can't wish for them back. Simple, 
straightforward, and adds another useful dimension with already existing 
items in the game. More thinking is always good in Nethack.


